== Trivia ==
* {{e|The Stain}} is his posthumous version, who also shows up in [[Chapters#Chapter 2|Chapter 2]]. Polycephalus is one of four bosses to have their posthumous version in the same chapter, the others being {{e|Gemini}} having {{e|Blighted Ovum}} in [[Chapter 1]], {{e|Chub}} having {{e|Carrion Queen}} in Chapter 2 and the {{e|Tuff Twins}} having {{e|The Shell}} in [[Chapters|Chapter 2.5]].
** {{dlc|nr}} However, Polycephalus is the only one of them to have their posthumous version in the same environments as well, sharing both the {{s|Catacombs}} and the {{s|Flooded Caves}} with The Stain. The only difference is that The Stain can appear in {{s|Caves}} as well, where Polycephalus cannot.
*** {{dlc|r}} This is no longer the case as of [[Repentance]], since Polycephalus no longer appears in the Flooded Caves while The Stain no longer appears in The Catacombs.
**** This makes Polycephalus the only boss whose posthumous variation is more likely to be encountered than its normal variation, since it can only be encountered in the Catacombs, whereas the Stain can be encountered in the Caves and Flooded Caves.
* [[Wikipedia:Polycephaly|Polycephaly]] is the condition of having more than one head.
* Polycephalus shares his name with a [[Wikipedia:Echinocactus polycephalus|cactus]].
* Polycephalus is one of the four bosses that can be spawned by {{e|It Lives!}}, the other three being {{e|Chub}}, {{Dlc|r}}{{e|Fistula}} and {{e|Teratoma}}.
* {{dlc+|na+}} Prior to [[Booster Packs#Booster Pack #5|Booster Pack #5]], Red Champion Polycephalus could spawn {{e|Scarred Para-Bite}}s if he was fought in the {{s|Scarred Womb}}.{{dlc-}}

